# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# This file did not exist until 2026-10-04. Because both Dockerfiles build from
# the repository root, the daemon was receiving the entire tree — including
# web/node_modules, the local .env with real secrets, and .git. Dockerfile.web
# then ran `COPY web/ ./`, which on a Windows host overwrote the Linux
# node_modules with Windows binaries. Keep this file in sync with what the
# Dockerfiles actually COPY:
#
#   Dockerfile.api needs : go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, internal/
#   Dockerfile.web needs : web/package.json, web/package-lock.json, web/

# ── VCS, CI and editor state ───────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
.kilo

# ── Secrets: never hand these to the daemon ────────────────────────────
# Without this the build context (and therefore any image layer or build log
# that echoes it) contains the operator's live credentials.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
id_rsa*
# .env.example and deploy/.env.example are templates, not secrets, but no
# Dockerfile COPYs them either; they are kept out to keep the context small.

# ── Build artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The critical one: Dockerfile.web does `COPY web/ ./`, so without this a
# developer's host node_modules (possibly Windows binaries) lands on top of
# the npm ci output from the deps stage.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo
bin/
dist/

# ── Logs and scratch output ────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
**/*.log
scratch/

# ── Runtime data (uploaded documents, local var tree) ──────────────────
var/

# ── Not needed to build ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# None of the Dockerfiles COPY any of these; excluding them keeps the context
# small and keeps documentation and runbooks out of the image.
docs/
deploy/
scripts/
*.md
AUDIT*.md
Makefile